    <p>It also smooths the year. A recurring residential base plus a Town Madison commercial contract or two means you're not living and dying by the weather. The website is what builds both — and it's what keeps building them after you've stopped paying a lead service that only sent you whoever clicked first.</p>

    <p>There's a compounding effect that lead services can never give you. Every soft-wash, roof-algae, and concrete-cleaning page you publish keeps ranking and keeps converting, year after year, with no per-lead fee attached. The homeowner in Madison Park who finds your roof-algae page in year one tells a neighbor in year two, and that neighbor finds the same page. A lead service charges you again for every one of those clicks. A website you own charges you nothing after it's built. Over three or four seasons, that difference is the difference between renting your customers and owning a real marketing asset.</p>

